<p>So these SDKs have too few maintainers. But that doesn't fully explain why it seems to take so long for new features to get through the stack. My guess for that was that somewhere in the process between submission of the new idea and the formalization of the idea was a long discussion that took a million years. </p><h3 id="conventions-about-semantics">Conventions about Semantics</h3><p>So with this level of surface area across different frameworks and languages, it makes sense to concentrate the conversation about conventions in one place. That lives here: <a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions">https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions</a></p><p>If vendor debate is causing the slowdown, we should (in theory) see this slowdown in PRs here. Then you should see the slowdown basically propagate out. Spoiler alert, I was wrong about this. Big thanks to the OpenTelemetry people for having good conventions on labeling their PRs which made this much easier. </p><p>So if <code>semconv</code> is the slowdown, let's look at the slowest PRs there. </p>
